      "Practical view-buying considerations apply forcefully here. The DC Ranch and Silverleaf architectural control regimes restrict adjacent-lot development tightly, which means the view you tour today is more likely to be preserved long-term than at less-controlled communities. Verify the specific lot-by-lot view-easement language in the CC&Rs during diligence: it varies by sub-village.",
      "View-corridor inventory at the top of the DC Ranch price band tends to clear efficiently to a national buyer pool when the right home surfaces, but month-to-month inventory at this specific intersection (DC Ranch + mountain views + the buyer\u2019s desired size and finish level) can be genuinely thin. Be prepared for patience. Verify current inventory against ARMLS."
